I was playing an elven priest.  I found a general store on lvl 2.  Came 
in, picked up some cheap, blessed scroll.  I picked up some stuff around 
me and read this scroll.  Allowed me to ID few things, among them I 
chose the most expensive scroll, which happened to be blessed SoSC.  I 
waited until my dog came near me, read it, pointed to shopkeeper...

I was standing to far from the shopkeeper.

Ok.  I can't pay, but I there is still some hope.  I read all the 
unidentified scrolls, nothing helped.  As a last resort, I read some 
cursed spellbook.

It teleported me, paralysed, a little dog bit me twice, but the 
paralysis passed, I killed the dog, and few K's (I had to use healing 
spell twice) and escaped downstairs.  Pheew!

On level 3 i looked into my inventory.  I had some stolen blessed 
potion.  "If blessed it can't hurt me much".  Quaffed it and got 
blinded.  "No problem.  Blindness gets cured quickly".  I went few steps 
into the first corridor there was, bumped on some door.  Tried to open 
it.  It was locked.  Kicked it.

"How dare you...". You hear a zap, the wand hits you.  You hear a zap, 
the wand hits you.
Tried to pay, but didn't have enough money.
You hear a zap, the wand hits you.  You hear a zap, the wand hits you. 
You die.

We have this proverb in Poland "The stolen things won't feed you". 
Sadly true.

Zefcia, killed by a wand.


